  "worked_solution": "A biconditional expression $P\u21d4Q\u2261(P\u21d2Q)\u2227(Q\u21d2P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A\u21d4B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N$ if and only if $x\\in {3,7}.$\n\n- $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N$ is equivalent to $x\\in {3,7}.$\n\n- If $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N$ then $x\\in {3,7},$ and if $x\\in {3,7}$ then $x\\in {-1,0,3,7}\\cap N.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"",
